From 557c7c83a841a3fc44a46d56955ab6fc96174b2f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AmirSalahY <hello@noury.ch>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 15:53:27 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 10/15] chore: bump the Fig corpus to 2.692.3, and import it by
 bare specifier
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

2.692.0 added an exports map limited to "." and "./dynamic", so the deep import
"@withfig/autocomplete/build/index.js" stopped resolving — ERR_PACKAGE_PATH_NOT_EXPORTED
at startup, i.e. no completions at all, not merely a failing test. "." maps to
that same file and older versions resolve it via main, so the bare specifier
works either side of the change.

Gains 11 specs (herd, ollama, uv, eza, kotlinc, lvim, oci, ampx, sake, shasum,
sqlmesh); nothing removed, and all 93 snapshots still pass.

